[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626808126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2626808126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2626808126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ckek-","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T09:59:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T10:33:05Z","body":"`RigidBody2D` should not be moved by setting the position, please see [the documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_rigidbody2d.html), you need to apply forces instead to make it move","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626808126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627420008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627420008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627420008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cmz9o","user":{"login":"arthurwieb","id":105752158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBk2mXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105752158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb","html_url":"https://github.com/arthurwieb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T13:58:23Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T13:58:23Z","body":"thanks for the tip @AThousandShips. I checked the documentation about rigidbody and area2d signals and i didn't find anything about those two not interacting.\n\n> Emitted when a [Shape2D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_shape2d.html#class-shape2d) of the received body enters a shape of this area. body can be a [PhysicsBody2D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_physicsbody2d.html#class-physicsbody2d) or a [TileMap](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tilemap.html#class-tilemap). [TileMap](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tilemap.html#class-tilemap)s are detected if their [TileSet](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tileset.html#class-tileset) has collision shapes configured. Requires [monitoring](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_area2d.html#class-area2d-property-monitoring) to be set to true.\n\nI had no problem moving the object, just problem detecting it, since it is a PhysicsBody2D i think the area2d signal should be interacting with it.\n\nSorry if what i'm reporting is full nonsense, i'm relative new to godot, i've been testing things for a few months or so","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627420008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627430835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627430835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627430835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cm2mz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:03:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:03:28Z","body":"It says that:\n> It cannot be controlled directly, instead, you must apply forces to it (gravity, impulses, etc.), and the physics simulation will calculate the resulting movement, rotation, react to collisions, and affect other physics bodies in its path.\n\nIt could be made more explicit to say that it won't work correctly if you use it incorrectly, like:\n> Controlling a `RigidBody2D` directly will prevent normal physics from working on that body, for example interactions with other objects will not work correctly.\n\nSo some improvements to the description to make this more clear might be good","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627430835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627456640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627456640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627456640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cm86A","user":{"login":"arthurwieb","id":105752158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBk2mXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105752158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb","html_url":"https://github.com/arthurwieb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:15:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:15:20Z","body":"That could be a good idea!\n\nBut the main problem is why the signal from a Area2D does not detect it? Because it is just asking for a physicsbody2d, right?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627456640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627462296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627462296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627462296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cm-SY","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:17:30Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:17:30Z","body":"No it's because you're using the type wrong, `RigidBody2D` should be moved by applying forces to it, not assigning the position, see the [`RigidBody` tutorial](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.html) for more details about how to use it\n\nIt works with a `RigidBody2D` when it is moved correctly","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627462296/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627470511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627470511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627470511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnASv","user":{"login":"arthurwieb","id":105752158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBk2mXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105752158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb","html_url":"https://github.com/arthurwieb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arthurwieb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:20:51Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:20:51Z","body":"Ooh, right. I didn't think this could be the cause of the problem.\n\nWow, thanks a lot! I'll test it again! 🤙","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627470511/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627484426","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102214#issuecomment-2627484426","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214","id":2627484426,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnDsK","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:27:37Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:27:37Z","body":"As a brief explanation the `RigidBody` type moves by forces, and only updates things like movement when the physics simulation moves it, setting the position directly \"teleports\" it and prevents a lot of that functionality\n\nWhen needing things to be moved by forces like bounce etc. `RigidBody` should be used, if you need to move the body manually more you should use `CharacterBody`, in this case I think using a `RigidBody` with forces is best, and can be done automatically in some cases","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627484426/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]